{"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Creating-a-SmartCardConnection-to-a-YubiKey","title":"Creating a SmartCardConnection to a YubiKey","identifiers":["doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/SmartCardConnection","doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/USBSmartCardConnection","doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/LightningSmartCardConnection","doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WiredSmartCardConnection"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NFCSmartCardConnection"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The  NFCSmartCardConnection is short lived and should be closed as soon as the commands sent to the YubiKey have finished processing. It is up to the user of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the connection to close it when it no longer is needed. As long as the connection is open the NFC modal will cover the lower part of the iPhone screen."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"In addition to the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/NFCSmartCardConnection\/close(error:)","isActive":true},{"text":" method defined in the SmartCardConnection protocol the NFCSmartCardConnection has an additional ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"close(success:)"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"method that will close the connection and set the alertMessage of the NFC alert to the provided message."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"NFC is only supported on iPhones from iPhone 6 and forward. It will not work on iPads since there’s no NFC chip in